# Preserve user-supplied specification evidence as exact bytes on every OS.
docs/specifications/source/genesis.txt binary
docs/specifications/source/genesis2.txt binary
docs/specifications/source/genesis3.txt binary
docs/specifications/source/genesis4.txt binary
docs/specifications/source/technology_mining_addendum.txt binary

# The repository content manifest is a GENERATED file, and it is compared
# byte for byte against what the inventory tool produces.
#
# It has to be LF everywhere, for two reasons that are the same reason.
# The tool writes LF explicitly, so that a Windows run and a Linux run
# produce the same bytes. And git has to check it out as LF, so that the
# working tree and the commit agree: with core.autocrlf=true a Windows
# checkout would otherwise hand back CRLF, and the file would show as
# modified the moment it was regenerated.
#
# Without this the manifest gate passed on both operating systems and
# still described two different files.
registry/repository_content.tsv text eol=lf
